part.text:
Fixed. Two changes, no test files touched:

1. **`include/fmt/format.h`** — `write_nonfinite` was rewritten (by the buggy change) to apply the raw fill char manually, which zero-pads inf/nan (`00+nan`). Restored the `write_padded`-based implementation and added the zero-fill→space replacement for non-finite values:
   ```cpp
   // Replace '0'-padding with space for non-finite values.
   if (specs_copy.fill.size() == 1 && specs_copy.fill[0] == static_cast<Char>('0'))
     specs_copy.fill[0] = static_cast<Char>(' ');
   ```

2. **`include/fmt/core.h`** — `on_zero()` now only sets `align::numeric` when no explicit alignment was given, so `{:>+06}`, `{:<+06}`, `{:^+06}` keep their explicit alignment while the `0` fill is still applied to finite numerics (preserving `"000000"` for `"{:>06.0f}"`).

Result: `{:+06}` on NaN/inf now yields `  +nan` / `  +inf` per the docs, sign-aware zero padding for real numbers is unchanged. All 18 test suites pass in the container (the previously failing `format_nan`/`format_infinity` tests and the pre-existing `width` test now all pass).
